    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T13:35:24Z",
    "body": "Two more behaviours from a parallel verification (#267, closed as duplicate): -l 3,0 silently ignores the index and assesses the whole file (samples = 0 is the no-subset sentinel), and -l 1,700000 on a 1,000,000-byte file loads 300,000 samples with only the generic '< 1000000 samples' warning. Observed: -l 4,4611686018427387904 (4 × 2^62 = 2^64) reads block 0 and reports the whole-file figure 0.82967708323411438; -l 1,1000 records the whole-file SHA-256 f9ea8832…b2313 while the subset's is 0c754070…8907.",
